{"name":"Geyser Basin","hex":"#e3cab5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"geyser","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A boiling natural spring which throws forth jets of water, mud, etc., at frequent intervals, driven upwards by the expansive power of steam.","A momentary vertical jet or fountain of fluid driven upwards by a violent force."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To (cause to) rush or burst upward like water from a geyser."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/geyser"},{"term":"basin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wide bowl for washing, sometimes affixed to a wall.","A shallow bowl used for a single serving of a drink or liquidy food."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To create a concavity or depression in.","To serve as or become a basin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Drumheller Fountain","blocks":[{"text":"Drumheller Fountain is an outdoor fountain on the University of Washington campus in Seattle, Washington, in the United States. The fountain was given its name in 1961 to honor the University Regent Joseph Drumheller, who gifted the central fountain machinery to the University for its centennial celebration."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/MK03244_University_of_Washington_Drumheller_Fountain.jpg/330px-MK03244_University_of_Washington_Drumheller_Fountain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drumheller_Fountain"},{"title":"Geyser","blocks":[{"text":"A geyser is a spring with an intermittent water discharge ejected turbulently and accompanied by steam. The formation of geysers is fairly rare and is caused by particular hydrogeological conditions that exist only in a few places on Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Yellowstone_National_Park_%28WY%2C_USA%29%2C_Old_Faithful_Geyser_--_2022_--_2599.j